+ - `tessellate.Flow.wrap[textual: Textual { type Result = Char }](content: textual, width: Int, hyphen: Text = t"-")(using Text is Measurable, Hyphenation): Sequence[textual]`

-   gains a fourth defaulted parameter, `unbreakable: List[denominative.Interval] = Nil`, in its
-   first clause. Each interval is a span of char offsets into `content.plain` within which no
-   soft break (space or hyphenation point) is taken; hard breaks inside one still break the
-   line. With the default the behaviour is unchanged. (#2121)
+   gana un cuarto parámetro con valor por defecto, `unbreakable: List[denominative.Interval] = Nil`,
+   en su primera cláusula. Cada intervalo es un tramo de desplazamientos de caracteres dentro de
+   `content.plain` en el que no se toma ningún salto blando (espacio o punto de división silábica);
+   los saltos duros dentro de él siguen partiendo la línea. Con el valor por defecto, el
+   comportamiento no cambia. (#2121)

- ## turbulence
+ ## turbulence

- - `turbulence.load` (the extension `value.load[result <: Documentary]`) no longer takes context
-   parameters. It was `def load[result <: Documentary](using streamable: (value is Streamable by
-   Text over Credit)^, loadable: (result is Loadable by Text)^): Document[result]`; it is now
-   `inline def load[result <: Documentary]: Document[result]`, resolving its instances with
-   `summonFrom` in this order: `value is Streamable by Data over Credit` with `result is Loadable
-   by Data`, else with `result is Loadable by Text` through a `hieroglyph.Charset` and a
-   `zephyrine.Buffering`; then `value is Streamable by Text over Credit` with `Loadable by Text`,
-   else with `Loadable by Data` through a `hieroglyph.Codepage` and a `Buffering`; then `value is
-   Readable to Data` (a whole-value source such as a `galilei.Path`) with the same two `Loadable`
-   alternatives. A text source whose `Streamable by Data` instance applies (a `Text` with a
-   `Codepage` in scope) therefore now takes the byte route, as `read` does. Code that passed the
-   context arguments explicitly must drop them; code that summoned `load`'s instances by hand
-   is unaffected (`Loadable` is unchanged). The new helpers `turbulence.Loadable.fromData[result](consume stream: (Stream[Data] over Credit)^): Document[result]`
-   and `Loadable.fromText[result](consume stream: (Stream[Text] over Credit)^): Document[result]`
-   are the per-operand halves of that dispatch. (#2118)
+ - `turbulence.load` (la extensión `value.load[result <: Documentary]`) ya no toma parámetros
+   contextuales. Era `def load[result <: Documentary](using streamable: (value is Streamable by
+   Text over Credit)^, loadable: (result is Loadable by Text)^): Document[result]`; ahora es
+   `inline def load[result <: Documentary]: Document[result]`, y resuelve sus instancias con
+   `summonFrom` en este orden: `value is Streamable by Data over Credit` con `result is Loadable
+   by Data`, o si no con `result is Loadable by Text` a través de un `hieroglyph.Charset` y un
+   `zephyrine.Buffering`; después `value is Streamable by Text over Credit` con `Loadable by Text`,
+   o si no con `Loadable by Data` a través de un `hieroglyph.Codepage` y un `Buffering`; después
+   `value is Readable to Data` (una fuente de valor completo, como una `galilei.Path`) con las
+   mismas dos alternativas de `Loadable`. Por tanto, una fuente de texto a la que se aplica su
+   instancia `Streamable by Data` (un `Text` con un `Codepage` en el ámbito) toma ahora la ruta de
+   bytes, como hace `read`. El código que pasaba los argumentos contextuales explícitamente debe
+   quitarlos; el código que convocaba a mano las instancias de `load` no se ve afectado
+   (`Loadable` no cambia). Las nuevas funciones auxiliares
+   `turbulence.Loadable.fromData[result](consume stream: (Stream[Data] over Credit)^): Document[result]`
+   y `Loadable.fromText[result](consume stream: (Stream[Text] over Credit)^): Document[result]`
+   son las dos mitades, una por operando, de ese despacho. (#2118)

- ## ulysses
+ ## ulysses

- - `ulysses.BloomFilter.apply[element: Digestible](approximateSize: Int, targetErrorRate: 0.0 ~ 1.0)[algorithm <: Algorithm](using Hash in algorithm, Permit[HashWeakness[algorithm]]): BloomFilter[element, algorithm]`
+ - `ulysses.BloomFilter.apply[element: Digestible](approximateSize: Int, targetErrorRate: 0.0 ~ 1.0)[algorithm <: Algorithm](using Hash in algorithm, Permit[HashWeakness[algorithm]]): BloomFilter[element, algorithm]`

-   sizes the filter differently. Old: `bitSize = (-1.44·approximateSize·ln targetErrorRate).toInt`,
-   `hashCount = (bitSize/approximateSize·ln 2 + 0.5).toInt`. New: with `n = max(1, approximateSize)`
-   and `p = max(targetErrorRate, 2⁻⁵³)`, `bitSize = max(1, ceil(-n·ln p/(ln 2)²))` and
-   `hashCount = max(1, round(bitSize/n·ln 2))`. So `BloomFilter[Text](100, 0.01).bitSize` is 959
-   where it was 663, `(1000, 0.01)` gives 9586 where it was 6631, `(100, 0.001)` gives 1438 where
-   it was 994, and `hashCount` for `(10_000, 0.01)` is 7 where it was 5. The old sizing delivered
-   about four times the requested false-positive rate; the new one delivers the requested rate.
-   (#2126)
- - `ulysses.BloomFilter#+`, `#++` and `ulysses.BloomFilter#hits` derive an element's bit positions differently. Old:
-   the digests of `(0, value)`, `(1, value)`, … (as a `Digestible` tuple) were concatenated into a
-   `BigInt` whose successive remainders modulo `bitSize` were the positions. New: `h₁` and `h₂` are
-   the first and second big-endian 64-bit words of the element's digest (of the element alone; an
-   algorithm yielding fewer than 16 bytes is re-digested with a big-endian `Int` prefix of 1, 2, …
-   until 16 bytes are gathered), and position `i` for `i` in `0 until hashCount` is
-   `((h₁ + i·h₂) & Long.MaxValue) % bitSize`. For the same elements, `bits` therefore differs from
-   the previous version's; a filter whose `bits` were persisted or exchanged with code built
-   against the old version must be rebuilt. (#2126)
- - `ulysses.BloomFilter[element, algorithm]` is no longer a `case class`; it is
-   `class BloomFilter[element: Digestible, algorithm <: Algorithm] extends caps.Mutable` with a
-   private constructor. Removed with the case class: the public constructor
+   dimensiona el filtro de otra manera. Antes: `bitSize = (-1.44·approximateSize·ln targetErrorRate).toInt`,
+   `hashCount = (bitSize/approximateSize·ln 2 + 0.5).toInt`. Ahora: con `n = max(1, approximateSize)`
+   y `p = max(targetErrorRate, 2⁻⁵³)`, `bitSize = max(1, ceil(-n·ln p/(ln 2)²))` y
+   `hashCount = max(1, round(bitSize/n·ln 2))`. Así, `BloomFilter[Text](100, 0.01).bitSize` es 959
+   donde era 663, `(1000, 0.01)` da 9586 donde daba 6631, `(100, 0.001)` da 1438 donde daba 994, y
+   `hashCount` para `(10_000, 0.01)` es 7 donde era 5. El dimensionado anterior daba
+   aproximadamente cuatro veces la tasa de falsos positivos solicitada; el nuevo da la tasa
+   solicitada. (#2126)
+ - `ulysses.BloomFilter#+`, `#++` y `ulysses.BloomFilter#hits` obtienen las posiciones de bits de
+   un elemento de otra manera. Antes: los resúmenes de `(0, value)`, `(1, value)`, … (como una tupla
+   `Digestible`) se concatenaban en un `BigInt` cuyos restos sucesivos módulo `bitSize` eran las
+   posiciones. Ahora: `h₁` y `h₂` son la primera y la segunda palabra de 64 bits big-endian del
+   resumen del elemento (del elemento solo; un algoritmo que da menos de 16 bytes se vuelve a
+   resumir con un prefijo `Int` big-endian de 1, 2, … hasta reunir 16 bytes), y la posición `i`
+   para `i` en `0 until hashCount` es `((h₁ + i·h₂) & Long.MaxValue) % bitSize`. Por tanto, para
+   los mismos elementos, `bits` difiere del de la versión anterior; un filtro cuyos `bits` se
+   persistieron o se intercambiaron con código compilado contra la versión anterior debe
+   reconstruirse. (#2126)
+ - `ulysses.BloomFilter[element, algorithm]` ya no es una `case class`; es
+   `class BloomFilter[element: Digestible, algorithm <: Algorithm] extends caps.Mutable` con un
+   constructor privado. Se eliminan con la case class: el constructor público

-   `BloomFilter(bitSize: Int, hashCount: Int, bits: scala.collection.immutable.BitSet)`, `copy`,
+   `BloomFilter(bitSize: Int, hashCount: Int, bits: scala.collection.immutable.BitSet)`, `copy`,

-   `unapply`, the field `bits: scala.collection.immutable.BitSet`, and `productElement`/
-   `productArity`. `bitSize: Int` and `hashCount: Int` remain as `val`s. `equals`/`hashCode`
-   compare `bitSize`, `hashCount` and the bits. New: `def population: Int`, the number of set
-   bits. (#2126)
+   `unapply`, el campo `bits: scala.collection.immutable.BitSet`, y `productElement`/
+   `productArity`. `bitSize: Int` y `hashCount: Int` se mantienen como `val`. `equals`/`hashCode`
+   comparan `bitSize`, `hashCount` y los bits. Nuevo: `def population: Int`, el número de bits
+   activados. (#2126)

- - `ulysses.BloomFilter.apply[element: Digestible](approximateSize: Int, targetErrorRate: 0.0 ~ 1.0)[algorithm <: Algorithm](using Hash in algorithm, Permit[HashWeakness[algorithm]])`
+ - `ulysses.BloomFilter.apply[element: Digestible](approximateSize: Int, targetErrorRate: 0.0 ~ 1.0)[algorithm <: Algorithm](using Hash in algorithm, Permit[HashWeakness[algorithm]])`

-   now returns `BloomFilter[element, algorithm]^` (an exclusive, mutable filter) where it returned
-   `BloomFilter[element, algorithm]`. New: `update def add(value: element): Unit` and
+   devuelve ahora `BloomFilter[element, algorithm]^` (un filtro exclusivo y mutable) donde
+   devolvía `BloomFilter[element, algorithm]`. Nuevos: `update def add(value: element): Unit` y

-   `update def addAll[collection: murmuration.Traversable by element](elements: collection): Unit`,
+   `update def addAll[collection: murmuration.Traversable by element](elements: collection): Unit`,

-   which set bits in place and are callable only on an exclusive filter, and
+   que activan bits en el sitio y solo pueden llamarse sobre un filtro exclusivo, y

-   `ulysses.BloomFilter.freeze[element, algorithm <: Algorithm](consume filter: BloomFilter[element, algorithm]^): BloomFilter[element, algorithm]^{}`,
+   `ulysses.BloomFilter.freeze[element, algorithm <: Algorithm](consume filter: BloomFilter[element, algorithm]^): BloomFilter[element, algorithm]^{}`,

-   which consumes the exclusive filter and yields the frozen (shareable, read-only) form without
-   copying. `+` and `++` now return `BloomFilter[element, algorithm]^{}` and copy the bits once;
-   `hits` is unchanged. Under capture checking, code that used one `BloomFilter[…]` value from
-   `apply` in several places (as a shared immutable value) must `freeze` it first, since an
-   exclusive value may not be aliased; code that only chains `apply(…) + x ++ xs` is unchanged.
-   Outside capture-checked code, nothing changes but the result types. (#2126)
- - `ulysses.BloomFilter#++(elements: Iterable[element]): BloomFilter[element, algorithm]` is now
+   que consume el filtro exclusivo y da la forma congelada (compartible y de solo lectura) sin
+   copiar. `+` y `++` devuelven ahora `BloomFilter[element, algorithm]^{}` y copian los bits una
+   vez; `hits` no cambia. Con comprobación de capturas, el código que usaba un mismo valor
+   `BloomFilter[…]` procedente de `apply` en varios lugares (como un valor inmutable compartido)
+   debe congelarlo antes con `freeze`, ya que un valor exclusivo no puede tener alias; el código
+   que solo encadena `apply(…) + x ++ xs` no cambia. Fuera del código con comprobación de
+   capturas, solo cambian los tipos de resultado. (#2126)
+ - `ulysses.BloomFilter#++(elements: Iterable[element]): BloomFilter[element, algorithm]` es ahora

-   `ulysses.BloomFilter#++[collection: murmuration.Traversable by element](elements: collection): BloomFilter[element, algorithm]`.
+   `ulysses.BloomFilter#++[collection: murmuration.Traversable by element](elements: collection): BloomFilter[element, algorithm]`.

-   A `scala.Iterable` argument is still accepted (through `Traversable.iterable`); the opaque
-   `proscenium.List`, `Sequence`, `Set`, `Chain` and a frozen `Array` are now accepted directly,
-   where previously they had to cross via `xs.stdlib`. (#2126)
- - `ulysses.BloomFilter.apply` with `approximateSize <= 0` or `targetErrorRate` of `0.0` or `1.0`
-   now yields a working filter (`bitSize >= 1`, `hashCount >= 1`; see the sizing entry). Old:
-   `approximateSize = 0` gave `hashCount = 0`, so `hits` was `true` for every element;
-   `targetErrorRate = 1.0` gave `bitSize = 0`, so `+`, `++` and `hits` threw
-   `java.lang.ArithmeticException`; `targetErrorRate = 0.0` gave `bitSize = Int.MaxValue`. (#2126)
- - `ulysses.Bibliography#lookup(prefix: Data): Iterator[Data]` yields the matching hashes in
-   ascending unsigned lexicographic byte order, where it previously yielded them in the order of
-   `Bibliography#hashes` (the order given to `Bibliography.apply(data: List[Data])`). The set
-   yielded is unchanged. `ulysses.Palimpsest#resolve` tries candidates in this order, so where a
-   signature decodes ambiguously against a library it may now resolve to a different sequence of
-   hashes. (#2141)
+   Se sigue aceptando un argumento `scala.Iterable` (a través de `Traversable.iterable`); los
+   opacos `proscenium.List`, `Sequence`, `Set`, `Chain` y un `Array` congelado se aceptan ahora
+   directamente, mientras que antes tenían que cruzar mediante `xs.stdlib`. (#2126)
+ - `ulysses.BloomFilter.apply` con `approximateSize <= 0` o con un `targetErrorRate` de `0.0` o
+   `1.0` da ahora un filtro que funciona (`bitSize >= 1`, `hashCount >= 1`; véase la entrada sobre
+   el dimensionado). Antes: `approximateSize = 0` daba `hashCount = 0`, así que `hits` era `true`
+   para todo elemento; `targetErrorRate = 1.0` daba `bitSize = 0`, así que `+`, `++` y `hits`
+   lanzaban `java.lang.ArithmeticException`; `targetErrorRate = 0.0` daba
+   `bitSize = Int.MaxValue`. (#2126)
+ - `ulysses.Bibliography#lookup(prefix: Data): Iterator[Data]` da los hashes coincidentes en orden
+   lexicográfico ascendente de bytes sin signo, mientras que antes los daba en el orden de
+   `Bibliography#hashes` (el orden dado a `Bibliography.apply(data: List[Data])`). El conjunto que
+   se da no cambia. `ulysses.Palimpsest#resolve` prueba los candidatos en este orden, así que,
+   cuando una signatura se decodifica de forma ambigua contra una biblioteca, puede resolverse
+   ahora a una secuencia de hashes distinta. (#2141)

- ## urticose
+ ## urticose

- - `urticose.Service` is now `case class Service(cancel: () => Unit, port: Int)`, where it was
-   `case class Service(cancel: () => Unit)`; `port` is the port the server is bound to.
-   Construction must supply it (the form `Service: () => …` no longer compiles), and an extractor
-   pattern `Service(cancel)` must become `Service(cancel, _)`. (#2151)
+ - `urticose.Service` es ahora `case class Service(cancel: () => Unit, port: Int)`, donde era
+   `case class Service(cancel: () => Unit)`; `port` es el puerto al que está ligado el servidor.
+   La construcción debe proporcionarlo (la forma `Service: () => …` ya no compila), y un patrón
+   extractor `Service(cancel)` debe pasar a ser `Service(cancel, _)`. (#2151)

- ## vivisection
+ ## vivisection

- - `vivisection.Debuggee(command, port = 0)` launches the debuggee with
-   `-agentlib:jdwp=…,address=*:0`, so the agent binds a free port of its own choosing, which the
-   session reads from the agent's `Listening for transport dt_socket at address: N` line on the
-   debuggee's standard output before attaching; previously a `port` of `0` attached to port 0 and
-   failed. The DAP adapter's `launch` request now uses this, rather than choosing a port by binding
-   and releasing a probe socket. (#2151)
+ - `vivisection.Debuggee(command, port = 0)` lanza el programa depurado con
+   `-agentlib:jdwp=…,address=*:0`, de modo que el agente liga un puerto libre elegido por él mismo,
+   que la sesión lee de la línea `Listening for transport dt_socket at address: N` del agente en la
+   salida estándar del programa depurado antes de adjuntarse; antes, un `port` de `0` se adjuntaba
+   al puerto 0 y fallaba. La petición `launch` del adaptador DAP usa ahora esto, en lugar de elegir
+   un puerto ligando y liberando un socket de sondeo. (#2151)

- ## xenophile
+ ## xenophile

- - Component `xenophile.lira` (artifact `xenophile-lira`) removed; it moved to the propensive/lira
-   repository with reliquary (see the reliquary entry). Its types — `CHeaderAtomizer`,
-   `CHeaderDiscipline`, `DtsAtomizer`, `DtsDiscipline`, `KotlinMetadataAtomizer`,
-   `KotlinMetadataDiscipline`, `WebIdlAtomizer`, `WebIdlDiscipline`, `WitAtomizer` and
-   `WitDiscipline` — move from package `xenophile` to package `lira`, unchanged in name and
-   signature, and are no longer exported into `soundness`. Depend on `dev.propensive:lira`
-   instead. (#2111)
+ - Se elimina el componente `xenophile.lira` (artefacto `xenophile-lira`); se ha trasladado al
+   repositorio propensive/lira junto con reliquary (véase la entrada de reliquary). Sus tipos
+   —`CHeaderAtomizer`, `CHeaderDiscipline`, `DtsAtomizer`, `DtsDiscipline`,
