- ## xylophone
+ ## xylophone

- - `xylophone.DynamicXmlEnabler` (and its `soundness` export) removed. Its replacement is
-   `xylophone.Xml is rudiments.Dynamical`. `xylophone.dynamicAccess.dynamicXml` is retained,
-   retyped from `DynamicXmlEnabler` to `Xml is Dynamical`. The erased parameter
-   `erased dynamicXmlEnabler: DynamicXmlEnabler` of `Xml#selectDynamic(name: String)` and
-   `Xml#applyDynamic(name: String)`, and the erased context parameter of the
-   `xylophone.xmlLens` given, are now `(? >: Xml) is Dynamical`. `dynamicXml` satisfies it,
-   and so does a `rudiments.dynamically[Xml]` or `dynamically` block. (#2102)
- - New codec givens in `object Xml`: `optionalDecodable`/`optionalEncodable` for any
-   `value >: Unset.type` with a `vacuous.Mandatable to inner` (i.e. `Optional[inner]`), and
-   `mapDecodable`/`mapEncodable` for `Map[key, value]`. A derived case class may now have
-   `Optional` and `Map` fields. An `Unset` field encodes to no child element (an `@Xml.attribute`
-   field to no attribute) and a missing element or attribute decodes to `Unset`; a `Map` field
-   encodes to one child element per entry holding `<key>` and `<value>` children, and gathers all
-   same-named children back. Previously such a field failed to derive, or (for `Optional[Text]`,
-   through the `Decodable in Text` bridge) raised `Xml.Error(Reason.Missing)` when absent.
-   `Optional[List[element]]` remains unsupported; use `List[element]`. (#2104)
- - New `xylophone.servables.xmlServable: (Codepage) => Xml is telekinesis.Servable` (media type
-   `application/xml; charset=UTF-8`), also exported as `soundness.servables.xmlServable`,
-   alongside the existing `xmlPostable`. (#2104)
- - New push form `xylophone.Xml.emit[medium: Xml.Emitter](document: turbulence.Document[Xml], deliver: medium => Unit)(using Xml.Formatting, zephyrine.Buffering): Unit`,
-   which serializes on the caller's thread with no fiber, handing each block to `deliver` as it
-   fills: `emit[Text]` delivers text blocks through a `Producer[Text]`, and `emit[Data]` delivers
-   UTF-8 bytes written directly by a byte-level serializer that escapes and encodes each string in
-   one pass. `trait Xml.Emitter[medium]` with givens `Xml.Emitter.text` and `Xml.Emitter.data`
-   selects between them. The type argument is required when `deliver` is an untyped lambda.
- - New `xylophone.Xml.lend(document: turbulence.Document[Xml])(lending: zephyrine.Producer.Lending[Data])(using Xml.Formatting, zephyrine.Buffering): Unit`,
-   the borrowing form of the push `emit`: each filled block of UTF-8 is lent as a
-   `zephyrine.Region[Data]` with its branded `Interval in region.type`, valid only for the
-   duration of the call, so nothing is copied; `emit[Data]` is defined over it and materializes
-   each block. The text of `show` and of the fiber form of `emit` is unchanged.
- - The annotations `xylophone.Xml.attribute`, `xylophone.Xml.xmlns` and `xylophone.Xml.unqualified`
-   are now reachable under `import soundness.*` as `@attribute`, `@xmlns(…)` and `@unqualified`,
-   as they already were under `import xylophone.*`. `xmlns` and `unqualified` are exported;
-   `attribute` is the type alias `soundness.attribute = xylophone.Xml.attribute`, so only the
-   annotation (type) resolves and the term `attribute` still names `galilei`'s and `tarantula`'s
-   methods. `@Xml.attribute` continues to work. (#1953)
- - `xylophone.Xml` is parsed from UTF-8 bytes. The `Aggregable` givens in `object Xml` that
-   were `by Text` are now `by Data` under their existing names — `Xml.aggregable`
-   (`(Xml of content) is Aggregable by Data`), `Xml.aggregable2` (`Xml is Aggregable by Data`)
-   and `Xml.aggregableParsed` (`(value in Xml) is Aggregable by Data`), and
-   `xylophone.Xml2.aggregableIn` (`(value in Xml) is Aggregable by Data`) — and
-   `Xml.readableParsed` is now `Data is Readable to (value in Xml)`. The `by Text` forms are
-   retained under new names, `Xml.aggregableText`, `Xml.aggregable2Text`,
-   `Xml.aggregableParsedText`, `Xml2.aggregableInText` and `Xml.readableParsedText`
-   (`Text is Readable to (value in Xml)`), with the same parameters as before; they encode the
-   text to UTF-8 and parse the bytes. A byte source (`path.read[Xml]`, an HTTP body) is
-   therefore parsed without a `hieroglyph.Charset` given and without decoding, and non-UTF-8
-   byte input must be decoded to `Text` by the caller first. Only code that names a given
-   changes. (#2116)
- - `xylophone.Xml.Issue` has a new case, `BadEncoding` (described as "the input is not valid
-   UTF-8"), raised in a `Parse.Error` when a slice of the input the parser keeps — a name, an
-   attribute value, character data, a comment, CDATA or a processing instruction — is not
-   well-formed UTF-8 (an overlong form, a surrogate, a value above U+10FFFF, a bad lead or
-   continuation byte). Such input was previously substituted by the `Charset`'s
-   `TextSanitizer` before parsing. Exhaustive matches on `Issue` need the case. (#2116)
- - `xylophone.Xml.Position` for a byte source counts bytes: `offset` and `length` are byte
-   offsets into the input, and the tracked `Xml.PositionIndex` lengths (`Document[Xml]#locate`)
-   are byte lengths. `column` counts code points (previously UTF-16 chars: an astral character
-   now advances it by one, not two). For a `Text` source, `offset` and `length` remain char
-   offsets into the text. All are unchanged for ASCII input. (#2116)
- - `xylophone.Xml.optionalDecodable` gains a leading `using` clause
+ - Se elimina `xylophone.DynamicXmlEnabler` (y su exportación en `soundness`). Su sustituto es
+   `xylophone.Xml is rudiments.Dynamical`. Se conserva `xylophone.dynamicAccess.dynamicXml`, con su
+   tipo cambiado de `DynamicXmlEnabler` a `Xml is Dynamical`. El parámetro borrado
+   `erased dynamicXmlEnabler: DynamicXmlEnabler` de `Xml#selectDynamic(name: String)` y
+   `Xml#applyDynamic(name: String)`, y el parámetro contextual borrado del given
+   `xylophone.xmlLens`, son ahora `(? >: Xml) is Dynamical`. `dynamicXml` lo satisface, y también
+   un bloque `rudiments.dynamically[Xml]` o `dynamically`. (#2102)
+ - Nuevos givens de códec en `object Xml`: `optionalDecodable`/`optionalEncodable` para cualquier
+   `value >: Unset.type` con un `vacuous.Mandatable to inner` (es decir, `Optional[inner]`), y
+   `mapDecodable`/`mapEncodable` para `Map[key, value]`. Una case class derivada puede tener ahora
+   campos `Optional` y `Map`. Un campo `Unset` se codifica como ningún elemento hijo (un campo
+   `@Xml.attribute`, como ningún atributo) y un elemento o un atributo ausente se decodifica como
+   `Unset`; un campo `Map` se codifica como un elemento hijo por entrada que contiene los hijos
+   `<key>` y `<value>`, y vuelve a reunir todos los hijos con el mismo nombre. Antes, un campo así
+   no se podía derivar, o (para `Optional[Text]`, a través del puente `Decodable in Text`) lanzaba
+   `Xml.Error(Reason.Missing)` cuando faltaba. `Optional[List[element]]` sigue sin estar
+   soportado; se usa `List[element]`. (#2104)
+ - Nuevo `xylophone.servables.xmlServable: (Codepage) => Xml is telekinesis.Servable` (tipo de
+   medio `application/xml; charset=UTF-8`), exportado también como
+   `soundness.servables.xmlServable`, junto al `xmlPostable` ya existente. (#2104)
+ - Nueva forma de inserción `xylophone.Xml.emit[medium: Xml.Emitter](document: turbulence.Document[Xml], deliver: medium => Unit)(using Xml.Formatting, zephyrine.Buffering): Unit`,
+   que serializa en el hilo del llamante sin ninguna fibra, y entrega cada bloque a `deliver` a
+   medida que se llena: `emit[Text]` entrega bloques de texto a través de un `Producer[Text]`, y
+   `emit[Data]` entrega bytes UTF-8 escritos directamente por un serializador a nivel de bytes que
+   escapa y codifica cada cadena en una sola pasada. `trait Xml.Emitter[medium]`, con los givens
+   `Xml.Emitter.text` y `Xml.Emitter.data`, elige entre ellos. El argumento de tipo es obligatorio
+   cuando `deliver` es una lambda sin tipos.
+ - Nuevo `xylophone.Xml.lend(document: turbulence.Document[Xml])(lending: zephyrine.Producer.Lending[Data])(using Xml.Formatting, zephyrine.Buffering): Unit`,
+   la forma de préstamo del `emit` de inserción: cada bloque lleno de UTF-8 se presta como una
+   `zephyrine.Region[Data]` con su `Interval in region.type` con la marca, válida solo mientras dura
+   la llamada, así que no se copia nada; `emit[Data]` se define sobre él y materializa cada bloque.
+   El texto de `show` y el de la forma con fibra de `emit` no cambian.
+ - Las anotaciones `xylophone.Xml.attribute`, `xylophone.Xml.xmlns` y `xylophone.Xml.unqualified`
+   son ahora accesibles con `import soundness.*` como `@attribute`, `@xmlns(…)` y `@unqualified`,
+   como ya lo eran con `import xylophone.*`. `xmlns` y `unqualified` se exportan; `attribute` es
+   el alias de tipo `soundness.attribute = xylophone.Xml.attribute`, así que solo se resuelve la
+   anotación (el tipo), y el término `attribute` sigue nombrando los métodos de `galilei` y de
+   `tarantula`. `@Xml.attribute` sigue funcionando. (#1953)
+ - `xylophone.Xml` se analiza a partir de bytes UTF-8. Los givens `Aggregable` de `object Xml` que
+   eran `by Text` son ahora `by Data` con sus nombres actuales —`Xml.aggregable`
+   (`(Xml of content) is Aggregable by Data`), `Xml.aggregable2` (`Xml is Aggregable by Data`) y
+   `Xml.aggregableParsed` (`(value in Xml) is Aggregable by Data`), y
+   `xylophone.Xml2.aggregableIn` (`(value in Xml) is Aggregable by Data`)—, y
+   `Xml.readableParsed` es ahora `Data is Readable to (value in Xml)`. Las formas `by Text` se
+   conservan con nombres nuevos, `Xml.aggregableText`, `Xml.aggregable2Text`,
+   `Xml.aggregableParsedText`, `Xml2.aggregableInText` y `Xml.readableParsedText`
+   (`Text is Readable to (value in Xml)`), con los mismos parámetros que antes; codifican el texto
+   en UTF-8 y analizan los bytes. Por tanto, una fuente de bytes (`path.read[Xml]`, un cuerpo HTTP)
+   se analiza sin un given `hieroglyph.Charset` y sin decodificar, y el llamante debe decodificar
+   antes a `Text` una entrada de bytes que no sea UTF-8. Solo cambia el código que nombra un given.
+   (#2116)
+ - `xylophone.Xml.Issue` tiene un caso nuevo, `BadEncoding` (descrito como "the input is not valid
+   UTF-8"), que se lanza en un `Parse.Error` cuando un trozo de la entrada que el analizador
+   conserva —un nombre, un valor de atributo, datos de caracteres, un comentario, CDATA o una
+   instrucción de procesamiento— no es UTF-8 bien formado (una forma sobrelarga, un sustituto, un
+   valor por encima de U+10FFFF, un byte inicial o de continuación incorrecto). Antes, una entrada
+   así la sustituía el `TextSanitizer` del `Charset` antes del análisis. Las coincidencias de
+   patrones exhaustivas sobre `Issue` necesitan el caso. (#2116)
+ - `xylophone.Xml.Position` cuenta bytes para una fuente de bytes: `offset` y `length` son
+   desplazamientos de bytes dentro de la entrada, y las longitudes registradas de
+   `Xml.PositionIndex` (`Document[Xml]#locate`) son longitudes en bytes. `column` cuenta puntos de
+   código (antes, caracteres UTF-16: un carácter astral la hace avanzar ahora en uno, no en dos).
+   Para una fuente `Text`, `offset` y `length` siguen siendo desplazamientos de caracteres dentro
+   del texto. Todos ellos no cambian para una entrada ASCII. (#2116)
+ - `xylophone.Xml.optionalDecodable` gana una cláusula `using` inicial

-   `(absence: distillate.Decodable.Absence in Xml, fault: distillate.Decodable.Fault in Xml,
+   `(absence: distillate.Decodable.Absence in Xml, fault: distillate.Decodable.Fault in Xml,

-   tactic: contingency.Tactic[Xml.Error])`. Behaviour under the companion defaults is unchanged.
-   New givens `xylophone.optionalityOptions.{strictXmlAbsence, lenientXmlAbsence, strictXmlFaults,
-   lenientXmlFaults}` (exported to `soundness.optionalityOptions`). (#2130)
+   tactic: contingency.Tactic[Xml.Error])`. El comportamiento con los valores por defecto del objeto
+   compañero no cambia. Nuevos givens
+   `xylophone.optionalityOptions.{strictXmlAbsence, lenientXmlAbsence, strictXmlFaults, lenientXmlFaults}`
+   (exportados a `soundness.optionalityOptions`). (#2130)

- ## ypsiloid
+ ## ypsiloid

- - `ypsiloid.DynamicYamlEnabler` (and its `soundness` export) removed. Its replacement is
-   `ypsiloid.Yaml is rudiments.Dynamical`. `ypsiloid.dynamicAccess.dynamicYaml` is retained,
-   retyped from `DynamicYamlEnabler` to `Yaml is Dynamical`. The erased parameter
-   `(using erased dynamicYamlEnabler: DynamicYamlEnabler)` of `Yaml#selectDynamic`,
-   `Yaml#applyDynamic`, `Yaml#update` and both `Yaml#updateDynamic` overloads, and the erased
-   context parameter of the `Yaml.lens` given, are now `(? >: Yaml) is Dynamical`.
-   `dynamicYaml` satisfies it, and so does a `rudiments.dynamically[Yaml]` or `dynamically`
-   block. (#2102)
- - New `ypsiloid.postables.yamlPostable: (Codepage, Yaml.Formatting) => Yaml is telekinesis.Postable`
-   and `ypsiloid.servables.yamlServable: (Codepage, Yaml.Formatting) => Yaml is telekinesis.Servable`
-   (media type `application/yaml; charset=UTF-8`), also exported as
-   `soundness.postables.yamlPostable` and `soundness.servables.yamlServable`. The `ypsiloid.http`
-   module now depends on `telekinesis.core` and, like `jacinta.http`, is JVM-only, so
-   `ypsiloid.construables.yamlConstruable` is no longer available on Scala.js. (#2104)
- - `ypsiloid.Yaml.optional` and `Yaml.option` gain a leading `using` clause
+ - Se elimina `ypsiloid.DynamicYamlEnabler` (y su exportación en `soundness`). Su sustituto es
+   `ypsiloid.Yaml is rudiments.Dynamical`. Se conserva `ypsiloid.dynamicAccess.dynamicYaml`, con su
+   tipo cambiado de `DynamicYamlEnabler` a `Yaml is Dynamical`. El parámetro borrado
+   `(using erased dynamicYamlEnabler: DynamicYamlEnabler)` de `Yaml#selectDynamic`,
+   `Yaml#applyDynamic`, `Yaml#update` y las dos sobrecargas de `Yaml#updateDynamic`, y el parámetro
+   contextual borrado del given `Yaml.lens`, son ahora `(? >: Yaml) is Dynamical`. `dynamicYaml` lo
+   satisface, y también un bloque `rudiments.dynamically[Yaml]` o `dynamically`. (#2102)
+ - Nuevos `ypsiloid.postables.yamlPostable: (Codepage, Yaml.Formatting) => Yaml is telekinesis.Postable`
+   y `ypsiloid.servables.yamlServable: (Codepage, Yaml.Formatting) => Yaml is telekinesis.Servable`
+   (tipo de medio `application/yaml; charset=UTF-8`), exportados también como
+   `soundness.postables.yamlPostable` y `soundness.servables.yamlServable`. El módulo
+   `ypsiloid.http` depende ahora de `telekinesis.core` y, como `jacinta.http`, es solo para la JVM,
+   así que `ypsiloid.construables.yamlConstruable` ya no está disponible en Scala.js. (#2104)
+ - `ypsiloid.Yaml.optional` y `Yaml.option` ganan una cláusula `using` inicial

-   `(absence: distillate.Decodable.Absence in Yaml, nullity: distillate.Decodable.Nullity in Yaml,
+   `(absence: distillate.Decodable.Absence in Yaml, nullity: distillate.Decodable.Nullity in Yaml,

-   fault: distillate.Decodable.Fault in Yaml, tactic: contingency.Tactic[Yaml.Error])` (previously
-   `optional` took `(tactic: Tactic[Yaml.Error])` and `option` nothing); `Yaml.option`'s result
-   type is now `(Option[value] is Decodable in Yaml)^{tactic}`. A YAML `null` in an
-   `Optional[T]` field now reads as `Unset` where it was previously passed to the inner decoder
-   (`Yaml.Error(Reason.NotType(Null, …))`); `Option[T]` already read it as `None`. New givens
-   `ypsiloid.optionalityOptions.{strictYamlAbsence, lenientYamlAbsence, strictYamlNulls,
-   lenientYamlNulls, strictYamlFaults, lenientYamlFaults}` (exported to
-   `soundness.optionalityOptions`). (#2130)
